  "details": "<p>The archaeological site of Gobero in modern Niger consists of approximately 200 burials and associated settlements. Three phases of substantial occupation extend from 7700 BCE to 2500 BCE, with a hiatus from 6200 BCE to 5200 BCE. During these periods the site was on the shore of a lake that subsequently became arid. A fourth phase is typified by transient occupation and ends in the fourth century BCE.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A settlement and cemetery in use from ca. 8000 BCE into the first millennium.",
